      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "encouraging_interaction",
      "label": "Motivational encouragement in public settings",
      "description": "The concept of a public figure encouraging children to believe in themselves is a common trope in media and charity work. It is often used to promote self-confidence, resilience, and social mobility. The meme relies on this cultural understanding that such interactions are meant to be uplifting and inspirational, not merely casual.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
